  - key: VIP_REWARDS_FAQ_COUNT
    value: 6
  - key: VIP_REWARDS_QUESTION_1
    value: <style=brown>What is Rewards Program?
  - key: VIP_REWARDS_ANSWER_1
    value: "Rewards Program is our fun and rewarding player loyalty program.\nPlayers
      earn Rewards Points through game play and purchases in order to receive exclusive
      in-game benefits and rewards. \nPlayers are automatically enrolled for free
      from their very first game!"
  - key: VIP_REWARDS_QUESTION_2
    value: <style=brown>How can I join Rewards Program?
  - key: VIP_REWARDS_ANSWER_2
    value: You are automatically enrolled as you begin playing Club Vegas.
  - key: VIP_REWARDS_QUESTION_3
    value: <style=brown>How do I earn Rewards Points?
  - key: VIP_REWARDS_ANSWER_3
    value: 'You can earn Rewards Points with every in-game purchase and level-up.

      Tapping
      on the ''Like & Get X'' button that slides down from the top of the screen
      also helps!'
  - key: VIP_REWARDS_QUESTION_4
    value: <style=brown>What are Tiers?
  - key: VIP_REWARDS_ANSWER_4
    value: 'In-game benefits and rewards get bigger and better as you progress through
      Tiers.

      Your Tier is based on the number of Rewards Points earned.


      Players
      receive bigger rewards and more in-game benefits by moving up through the 21
      tiers:

      Bronze-1,2,3, Silver-1,2,3, Gold-1,2,3, Emerald-1,2,3, Ruby-1,2,3,
      Sapphire-1,2,3 and Diamond-1,2,3.'
  - key: VIP_REWARDS_QUESTION_5
    value: <style=brown>Are Rewards Points redeemable?
  - key: VIP_REWARDS_ANSWER_5
    value: No. You cannot redeem or cash out your Rewards Points in any way.
  - key: VIP_REWARDS_QUESTION_6
    value: <style=brown>Are Rewards Points transferable?
  - key: VIP_REWARDS_ANSWER_6
    value: No. Rewards Points are specific to each account and are not transferable
      to any other account.
  - key: CLUB_FAQ_COUNT
    value: 15
  - key: CLUB_FAQ_QUESTION_0
    value: <style=brown>What is a Club?
  - key: CLUB_FAQ_ANSWER_0
    value: "Club is a player's community, providing a joy of cooperation. \nThere
      will be an Epic Win bonus for Club members when a member hits an Epic Win.\nYou
      can team up with other players and grow Club together so that Club can have
      more members.\nAlso, you can chat with Club members, while you are playing
      any slot. \nA lot of fun updates like Club challenge that all Club members
      can enjoy together will be updated soon. "
  - key: CLUB_FAQ_QUESTION_1
    value: <style=brown>How to join a Club?
  - key: CLUB_FAQ_ANSWER_1
    value: 'If you want to join a Club, go to Club Main page.

      The "Join Club"
      screen with available Clubs will be displayed only if you''re not already a
      Club member.

      There will be a welcome bonus for player who join the Club
      first time.'
  - key: CLUB_FAQ_QUESTION_2
    value: <style=brown>How to start my own Club?
  - key: CLUB_FAQ_ANSWER_2
    value: 'You can create your own Club, if you can''t find the right Club for you.

      Go
      to Club Main page and find the "CREATE CLUB" button on the top right corner.

      Creating
      a Club costs <style=coin>{0:CommaNumber}</style> coins. If you decide to create
      a Club, you can set up Club name, Message of the day, and symbol icon. '
  - key: CLUB_FAQ_QUESTION_3
    value: <style=brown>How do I leave a Club?
  - key: CLUB_FAQ_ANSWER_3
    value: 'To leave your current Club, go to the settings menu and pick the last
      position from the list,

      you will be asked to confirm if you want to
      leave the Club. This option is only available if you go to settings menu while
      being on the Club page.'
  - key: CLUB_FAQ_QUESTION_4
    value: <style=brown>Club Level
  - key: CLUB_FAQ_ANSWER_4
    value: 'The Club level depends on the amount of total donation.

      Leveling
      up is done automatically when the required amount of coins is gathered.

      Every
      member will be notified about the upgrade by a pop-up on the next visit to
      the Club.

      To see how many coins are required for the next upgrade,

      you
      need to tap the question mark button near the Donation icon. Currently, maximum
      Club Level is {0}.'
  - key: CLUB_FAQ_QUESTION_5
    value: <style=brown>Club Donations
  - key: CLUB_FAQ_ANSWER_5
    value: 'Donations are made to level the Club up. Each level has a limit amount
      of daily donation.

      To donate, you need to press the "DONATE" button
      located in the bottom-right corner of the Club Lobby.

      Then popup will
      be appeared. You can donate the max possible amount at once, but also an option
      to donate a less-than-maximum amount.'
  - key: CLUB_FAQ_QUESTION_6
    value: <style=brown>Club captain
  - key: CLUB_FAQ_ANSWER_6
    value: 'Each Club has a captain, who manage a Club and can kick out players from
      Club.

      If a Club has members more than one and the captain want to get
      out of his/her own Club,

      the next player who joined the Club earliest
      will be promoted to captain.

      If a Club has no member without a captain
      and captain want to leave the Club, the Club will be removed.'
  - key: CLUB_FAQ_QUESTION_7
    value: <style=brown>Club chat, Newsfeed and Epic Win bonus
  - key: CLUB_FAQ_ANSWER_7
    value: 'You can communicate with other Club members in 2 ways: Club Chat, Club
      News Feed.

      The Club Chat is more casual and ephemeral, while the Club
      News Feed is a place where Club Members may share important news.

      The
      Club News Feed is also a place where Club Members collect Epic Win Bonuses
      resulting Epic Wins other members hit.

      If a Club member hit an Epic
      Win, the Epic Win screen will be shared in Club News Feed and other members
      can get Epic Win bonuses by liking it.'
  - key: CLUB_FAQ_QUESTION_8
    value: <style=brown>Club Challenge
  - key: CLUB_FAQ_ANSWER_8
    value: "Club challenges are daily missions you can complete together with your
      club members. \nPlay together in a club to complete them and get awesome rewards!"
  - key: CLUB_FAQ_QUESTION_9
    value: <style=brown>What is Epic League for Club?
  - key: CLUB_FAQ_ANSWER_9
    value: 'You can compete with other Clubs in Epic league to win great prizes!

      Rank
      higher to win bigger prizes and rise up to higher tier.'
  - key: CLUB_FAQ_QUESTION_10
    value: <style=brown>How do I participate in Epic League?
  - key: CLUB_FAQ_ANSWER_10
    value: "First, join a Club if you're not in one already.\nNext, start spinning
      to participate in the Epic league! \nThe Clubs with the most League Points
      at the end of the Epic league will rank highest and win the biggest prizes."
  - key: CLUB_FAQ_QUESTION_11
    value: <style=brown>When do Epic Leagues run?
  - key: CLUB_FAQ_ANSWER_11
    value: 'Epic Leagues typically start and end on Monday each week.

      You
      can check at league page when this week''s Epic League will end.'
  - key: CLUB_FAQ_QUESTION_12
    value: <style=brown>What are Club Points?
  - key: CLUB_FAQ_ANSWER_12
    value: "League Points determine ranks in Epic league - the Clubs with the most
      League Points earned during\nthat week's league will receive higher ranks and
      bigger prizes!\nhe more you win, the more League Points you earn!\nDo you need
      League Points fast? Try betting higher to win more faster!\nThere are also
      events where LPs earned get boosted by 2x or more so be sure to spin more during
      those times!\nEven if a Club member leaves or is removed from the Club, the
      League Points they have earned remains still.\nBesides determining ranks in
      Epic League, League Points are also needed to complete the Club Challenges\n
      - a different amount for each challenge. Complete the Challenges to collect
      League point bonuses."
  - key: CLUB_FAQ_QUESTION_13
    value: <style=brown>What are Club Tiers?
  - key: CLUB_FAQ_ANSWER_13
    value: "Clubs only compete with other Clubs in the same Club Tier during the
      weekly Epic League.\nClub Tiers are adjusted at the end of each Epic League,
      with League ranks determining the next week's Club Tiers.\nClubs in the top
      2 ranks of their Club Tier at the end of a Epic League will be moved up to
      the next Tier, \nfor a chance at even better prizes.\nClubs below the top 4
      ranks of their Club Tier at the end of a Epic League will be moved down a Club
      Tier, \nallowing them to compete with Clubs more similar to their own, for
      a chance at higher ranks.\nNo matter the Club Tier or rank, all Clubs will
      earn a prize at the end of the Epic League."
  - key: CLUB_FAQ_QUESTION_14
    value: <style=brown>How many co-captains can a club have?
  - key: CLUB_FAQ_ANSWER_14
    value: 'Each club can have co-captains according to the club level:

      Club
      levels 1 to 3= 1 Co-captain

      Club levels 4&5= 2 Co-captains

      Club
      levels 6&7= 3 Co-captains

      Club levels 8&9= 4 Co-captains

      Club
      levels 10&11= 5 Co-captains

      Club levels 12&13= 6 Co-captains

      Club
      levels 14&15= 7 Co-captains

      Club levels 16&17= 8 Co-captains

      Club
      levels 18&19= 9 Co-captains

      Club levels 20 or higher= 10 Co-captains'
